      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-72726: the coefficient matrix has determinant 7, giving the inverse and matrix product in option 0; the solution is (1,-1). q-78549: substitution gives (0,-3,1), whose sum is -2. q-78552: (1,2,-1) satisfies all three equations and sums to 2. q-42449: rearranging gives 2x+z=3, 3x+5y-2z=2, and 2x-2y+3z=1; (4,-4,-5) satisfies these and sums to -5. q-78559 and q-78561: multiplying both sides on the left by D^{-1} gives D^{-1}D=I_n; the respective missing parts are D^{-1}, I_n and D^{-1}, q. The displayed incomplete derivations are interpreted using their requested missing parts and complete worked derivations. q-73289: the antiderivative is cot(x), so the integral is -1-sqrt(3)/3. q-12965, q-12960, and q-135995: the quadratic coefficients are binomial(9,2)=36, binomial(7,2)6^2=756, and binomial(7,2)(-2/3)^2=28/3. q-136014: binomial(14,3)(-1/2)^3=-91/2. Continuity gives q-152757=0, q-152804=3pi/2+3(pi/6)=2pi, and q-149958=tan((2pi/3)/2)=sqrt(3). q-142097 and q-109942 simplify to y>2x-3 and y>x/2+2; both require dashed boundaries and shading above. Their selected unannotated images depict the same regions as the annotated worked-solution images. Every MA answer below is supported by its own verbatim worked-solution span; no grade evidence is supplied.",
